192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 127 0 R
/E (In modern surveillance, autonomous navigation, defense, and terrain-mapping systems, maintaining stable sensor orientation is critical for ensuring accurate data collection and operational efficiency. Vehicle-mounted cameras and LiDAR sensors operating on rough or uneven terrain are constantly exposed to vibrations, shocks, tilts, and unpredictable motion disturbances. These external factors can significantly degrade image quality, reduce sensor accuracy, and compromise navigation or monitoring performance.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 127 0 R
/E (This project focuses on the development of a servo-actuated 3-axis stabilization platform specifically intended for vehicle-mounted cameras and LiDAR sensors in rough terrain applications. By integrating embedded control systems, real-time motion sensing, and multi-axis mechanical correction, the platform is designed to preserve sensor alignment and enhance data reliability under dynamic conditions.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
