268 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (The project successfully demonstrates the design and implementation of a 3-axis orientation stabilization platformusing embedded control and mechatronic principles. By utilizing real-time data from the MPU6050 sensor and applying a PID-based closed-loop control system, the platform effectively reduces disturbances in roll, pitch, and yaw, maintaining stable orientation under external motion.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
269 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (The system shows reliable performance in terms of fast response, minimal overshoot, and low steady-state error, validating the effectiveness of the control strategy and actuator design. MATLAB-based modeling and simulation further support the practical feasibility of the system.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
270 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (Overall, the project highlights the integration of control systems, embedded programming, and mechanical design to solve real-world stabilization problems, with strong potential for applications in robotics, autonomous systems, and sensor platforms operating in dynamic environments.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
